9. FOLLOW-UP after the blind re-review of 6b887576 (scratchpad/review-k058-followup.md).

   Review finding (MEDIUM): the tenant-scoped INNER JOIN withheld the foreign
   customer's name by DISCARDING the whole row, so company A's own R600 of AR
   vanished from the debtors table and the overdue list while still counting in
   getCollectionStats.totalOutstanding — i.e. the K-058 defect class reproduced
   in a narrower slice. Applied the reviewer's recommended form.

   Change: both `JOIN customers c` -> `LEFT JOIN customers c` (tenant predicate
   kept), projection `c.name` -> `COALESCE(c.name, 'Unknown customer')`, and the
   `FILTER (WHERE EXISTS ...)` guard on clientCount dropped (no longer needed:
   with an outer join every debtor group is listed, so a plain COUNT(DISTINCT)
   equals summary.length — collection-stats WHERE is character-identical to the
   summary WHERE, and COALESCE(client_id, customer_id) is never NULL because
   customer_id is NOT NULL).

