9b. Mutation proof, three separate mutations, each restored afterwards:
      LEFT JOIN -> JOIN (undo this follow-up)          5 failed | 4 passed
      drop `AND c.company_id = ci.company_id` (both)   1 failed | 8 passed
      COALESCE(client_id, customer_id) -> client_id    5 failed | 4 passed
    All three RED. The tenant-predicate mutation now fails only the name
    assertion (1 test) rather than 5, because with an outer join the row and its
    money stay visible either way — only the NAME leaks. That is the correct
    narrower blast radius, not a weaker test.

